---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Container from '../components/Container.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import AranduWordmark from '../components/AranduWordmark.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Leonardo Cardoso | Backend Engineer"
  description="Software engineer with 4+ years of production experience building backend APIs and cloud systems with Python, TypeScript, Rust, and AWS."
>
  <Container>
    <main>
      <header class="hero">
        <AranduWordmark size={32} />
        <h1>Leonardo Cardoso</h1>
        <p class="hero-role">Software engineer focused on backend systems</p>
        <p class="hero-summary">
          I have 4+ years of experience building and maintaining production APIs
          and cloud systems with Python, TypeScript/Node.js, Rust, and AWS.
          I have taken features from requirements discussions with product and
          clients through implementation, deployment, and production support.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-availability">
          Based in Brazil. Open to remote roles and contract work.
        </p>
        <nav class="contact-links" aria-label="Contact and professional profiles">
          <a href="mailto:leonardorudolfocardoso@gmail.com">Email →</a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/leonardo-rudolfo-cardoso-a8b420183/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/leonardorudolfocardoso" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>
        </nav>
      </header>

      <Section title="Professional experience">
        <div class="experience">
          <article>
            <h3>Arqgen</h3>
            <p class="experience-role">Software Developer · Aug 2022 – Jan 2026</p>
            <ul class="experience-details">
              <li>
                Led delivery of a warehouse budget-estimation product from
                requirements through client reviews, and built its Tokio-based
                Rust Lambda API for domain entities, budget calculations, and
                floor-plan elements.
              </li>
              <li>
                Built a Rust subscriber to map Autodesk-converted DWG geometry
                to domain entities, validate polygons and required layers, persist
                results to MongoDB, and report outcomes through AppSync GraphQL.
                Extended proprietary Rust geometry libraries with operations,
                bug fixes, and computation tests.
              </li>
              <li>
                Designed parallel Step Functions workflows, integrated an existing
                Rust CLI with Python subprocesses, and debugged serialization and
                timeout failures. Built EventBridge integrations to decouple
                asynchronous workflows.
              </li>
              <li>
                Maintained production Python and Node.js services and investigated
                issues with CloudWatch. Worked in an SST-based TypeScript monorepo
                for repeatable deployments and built custom Docker images for
                Python Lambda dependencies.
              </li>
              <li>
                Developed interactive React layout visualization and editing with
                react-konva and Chakra UI, replacing static images with selectable
                objects and editable dimensions. Integrated APIs and WebSockets
                and fixed production frontend bugs.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Hype Empreendimentos</h3>
            <p class="experience-role">Junior Software Developer · Mar 2021 – Aug 2022</p>
            <ul class="experience-details">
              <li>
                Built a NestJS and TypeScript backend for an investing mobile
                application, applying TDD and separating business rules from
                framework and infrastructure concerns.
              </li>
              <li>
                Maintained internal Node.js APIs shipped through the team's GitLab
                CI pipelines. Extended a PostgreSQL-backed ETL pipeline with
                TypeScript, TypeORM, SQL joins, aggregations, and insert/update
                queries.
              </li>
              <li>
                Developed a property marketing website with Next.js Pages Router
                (SSG/ISR) and Chakra UI, integrating API-sourced listings and
                Strapi-managed content that updated without a code deployment.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </Section>

      <Section title="Education and research">
        <div class="experience">
          <article>
            <h3>Federal University of Santa Catarina (UFSC)</h3>
            <p class="experience-role">Bachelor's Degree in Civil Infrastructure Engineering · 2021</p>
            <ul class="experience-details">
              <li>
                <strong>XPS Peak Finder, 2018:</strong> Co-authored a research
                poster about GUI software for spectra analysis; received the
                Best Poster Award at the XII Encontro de Física do Instituto
                Tecnológico de Aeronáutica (ITA), 2018.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Undergraduate research, 2018–2019:</strong> Implemented
                and analyzed a C++ Lattice Boltzmann simulation to validate an
                experimental setup for microchannel flows.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Linear Algebra teaching assistant:</strong> Selected by
                academic performance for three semesters. Helped prepare exercise
                lists in LaTeX and supported students with problem solving and
                explanations of concepts.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </Section>
    </main>

    <footer class="footer">
      <p>© 2026 Leonardo Cardoso</p>
    </footer>
  </Container>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-block: 4rem 2rem;
  }

  h1 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .hero-role {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 3vw, 1.4rem);
  }

  .hero-summary {
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .hero-availability {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .contact-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem 2rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .contact-links a {
    padding-block: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.3em;
    transition: color var(--transition);
  }

  .contact-links a:hover {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .contact-links a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .experience {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    max-width: 65ch;
  }

  .experience h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .experience p {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .experience .experience-role {
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .experience-details {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .experience-details strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .footer {
    padding-block: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
</style>
